cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "AKANE Architecture E2: Finding an LLM's mistakes from how its answers connect"
abstract: >-
  Code, data, and results for small experiments in which a small language model
  (Gemma-2 2B) answers many true/false statements and writes its own consistency
  rules, some of them wrong. A network checks the model's answers against those
  rules while also doubting each rule, using belief propagation, and the signals
  are compared with the model's confidence and with counting rule violations.
authors:
